    <p>I’m Evan DeLord. I started this site to share my thoughts and research on how AI behaves and how to better use it. My first exposure to agents and algorithms was <a href="https://direct.mit.edu/isal/proceedings/alife2014/26/129/99060">doing research at UT Austin</a> in the field of <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_life">artificial life</a>, which uses simulated organisms to study evolution. Later, I researched <a href="https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/sciadv.aap9660">neural net simulations</a> of <a href="https://www.jneurosci.org/content/38/41/8831">the cerebellum</a> to better understand the principles of the brain.</p>
    <p>I wrote my undergraduate capstone thesis about the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Five_personality_traits">Big Five personality traits</a> and how personality might extend beyond these traits into values, goals, and self-narrative. Overall I’m really interested in emergent properties of complex systems, like computation in the brain or evolutionary processes.</p>
    <p>AI models have their own psychology and their own ways of communicating and interacting that are worth studying. We’re just beginning to understand what makes LLM-based AI tick and how to apply it. This site showcases my projects, built with <a href="https://claude.com/product/claude-code">Claude Code</a> and <a href="https://openai.com/codex/">Codex</a>, like <a href="/work/claude-autobiographies">the autobiography series</a> and <a href="/work/cabin-and-tower">the cabin and tower study</a>. Coding benchmarks are important, but trying to understand the models beyond benchmarks will matter for keeping AI helpful to humans.</p>
    <p>I’ve worked six years as an MLOps engineer at Chevron in trading. I now work as a Senior Cloud Engineer at Bosch, where AI integration is a big part of my work.</p>
    <p>I’m also an amateur meditator and I enjoy discussing philosophy and future predictions at my local Rationalist meetup. At the moment, I’m enjoying Budapest’s unique culture and ease of travel to the rest of Europe.</p>
    <p class="author-signature">-Evan</p>
